---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — Aleatory Spatial Memories"
  description="How Aleatory Spatial Memories handles Founding Captures application information."
>
  <main id="main" class="legal-page">
    <a class="legal-back" href="/">← Aleatory Spatial Memories</a>
    <p class="section-index">Privacy notice · v0</p>
    <h1>Application privacy</h1>
    <p class="legal-updated">Effective September 8, 2026</p>

    <section>
      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        If you apply for a Founding Capture, we collect the name, email address,
        general Connecticut-area location, scene description, scene categories,
        and optional practical details you submit. Please do not include
        sensitive information or private information about other people.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>How we use it</h2>
      <p>
        We use application information only to assess whether a proposed scene
        may fit the experimental program, respond to you, plan a possible
        conversation, and understand interest in the service. Applying does not
        grant permission to publish your story or capture. Any capture,
        testimonial, or publication permission will be discussed separately.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Where it goes</h2>
      <p>
        The form is processed by Cloudflare and delivered as an email to the
        founder’s Gmail account. The application Worker does not intentionally
        store a separate copy. Cloudflare, Google, and GitHub process limited
        technical or account data under their own terms and privacy practices.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Retention and choices</h2>
      <p>
        Application emails are retained only while useful for evaluating and
        operating the Founding Captures program. You may ask us to delete your
        application or stop contacting you by replying to our correspondence.
        More detailed capture terms will apply before any session involving
        people, homes, audio, or source imagery.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Privacy questions may be sent to
        <a href="mailto:aleatorydialogue@gmail.com"
          >aleatorydialogue@gmail.com</a
        >.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    min-height: 100vh;
    padding: clamp(2rem, 7vw, 7rem);
    background: var(--paper);
  }
  .legal-back {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: clamp(4rem, 10vw, 8rem);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-underline-offset: 0.25rem;
  }
  .legal-page h1 {
    max-width: none;
    margin: 1rem 0;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .legal-updated {
    color: #6a655b;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }
  .legal-page section {
    max-width: 48rem;
    margin: 3rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
  }
  .legal-page h2 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 400;
  }
  .legal-page section p {
    color: #514e46;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .legal-page section a {
    text-underline-offset: 0.2rem;
  }
</style>
